<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul bourse halts trading in Korea Long.</title>
<headline>Seoul bourse halts trading in Korea Long.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Stock Exchange suspended trading in shares of Korea Long Term Credit Bank in afternoon trading on Monday after the bank announced a huge bonus issue in August, a bourse statement said.  </p>
<p>Korea Long Term Credit Bank said it would offer a one-for-10 bonus issue in August.</p>
<p>Bank shares stood at 15,200 won before trading was suspended.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
